Z||000000||Monkeyman||07-02-2000||03:02 PM||||Actually it started out as my wifes dog since she got him just before we met.  His name is Cowboy and he's a full blooded German Shepherd.  He's been living down at my father in laws house in Oh since we didn't have any place to keep him up here.  Now that we have our fence done, my wife brought him up here.  The only problem is that he's very malnourished.  My sister in law has been taking care of him (or not).  You can see his ribs and he doesn't have much of a shine to his coat.  It's a good thing I don't want to go to jail 'cause I'm in a beating-up-my-sister-in-law mood right about now.<BR>Cowboy hasn't really seen me much so I figured it would take him a while to get used to me.  Not.  We're buddies already.  He really is a cool dog.  Real friendly.  He loves to get scratched on the sides of his neck.  Man.  What a feeling to be able to walk outside and have a dog run up to you like you're his best friend.  It's a great feeling to know that you're loved and wanted.<P>Forgive my ramblings.  <P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||10
